      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "WF1 - FRAME-BY-FRAME PANORAMA UPSCALE (writes to disk incrementally)\n\nRun this FIRST, then run 2b2_sfm_from_upscaled on the same dataset.\n\nHOW IT AVOIDS THE 163 GB OOM:\nThe Meta Batch Manager (frames_per_batch=1) makes ComfyUI re-run the whole rail\nONCE PER FRAME, so only a single 8K frame is ever in RAM. Each upscaled frame is\nwritten straight to disk by Save Upscaled Frames (Streaming). Nothing is held as\nan 81-frame 8K batch, so the CAS pre-sharpen no longer stacks 163 GB.\n\nWIRING NOTES:\n- Resolve Dataset Images -> dataset_name = your panorama_only dataset (e.g. dark-alley-02).\n  Its load_dir feeds the loader; its canonical_dir feeds the streaming saver, which\n  writes to <canonical>_upscaled (a NEW folder; your originals are never touched).\n- The throwaway VHS_VideoCombine is REQUIRED: VideoHelperSuite only keeps a meta-batch\n  loop requeueing when a VHS_VideoCombine is on the manager. It is fed the cheap\n  low-res frames and save_output=false, so it just advances the loop.\n- select_every_nth on the loader is 1 (upscale every panorama). The saver clears the\n  _upscaled folder on the first iteration, so re-running is safe/idempotent.\n\nSPEED: 81 frames x (RealESRGAN + 8K scale + SD tile refine) runs sequentially - this\nis slower than a batch, but it actually fits in memory and saves as it goes."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
